{"id": "h2-3A-01", "topic": "3A", "stem": "Which division of the autonomic nervous system regulates visceral functions during rest and digestion and has effects that oppose the fight-or-flight division?", "options": ["sympathetic nervous system", "sensory-somatic nervous system", "parasympathetic nervous system", "autonomic nervous system"], "answer": "parasympathetic nervous system", "source_id": "74c94ca4-7be1-5358-92de-9308edb48fa6", "source_span": {"chunk_id": "74c94ca4-7be1-5358-92de-9308edb48fa6#4620-5886", "start": 5069, "end": 5099, "quote": "parasympathetic nervous system", "block_id": null, "url": "https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/35-key-terms"}, "citation": "74c94ca4-7be1-5358-92de-9308edb48fa6[5069:5099] https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/35-key-terms", "generator": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-2025-08-07", "attempt_id": "300cd85de6a7", "target_concept": "Sympathetic and parasympathetic nervous systems: antagonistic control", "question_type": "an identification question - name the structure, molecule or term the passage describes", "prompt_sha256": "dc782a545791b55f6558591c1cccc84ef5fd5df2d61223ccc1849453e565fbfe", "generated_at": "2026-08-02T19:23:57Z", "status": "live"}
{"id": "h2-2C-02", "topic": "2C", "stem": "During early embryonic development, exposure to ionizing radiation causes DNA damage that activates p53. Which cell cycle regulatory protein then directly inhibits the cell cycle?", "options": ["p53", "retinoblastoma protein (Rb)", "E2F", "p21"], "answer": "p21", "source_id": "27082fea-78ab-5c36-9347-11c9fdedd944", "source_span": {"chunk_id": "27082fea-78ab-5c36-9347-11c9fdedd944#3405-4578", "start": 4481, "end": 4484, "quote": "p21", "block_id": null, "url": "https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/10-key-terms"}, "citation": "27082fea-78ab-5c36-9347-11c9fdedd944[4481:4484] https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/10-key-terms", "generator": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-2025-08-07", "attempt_id": "85a3f2f2b95c", "target_concept": "Environment–gene interaction in development", "question_type": "a mechanism question - what happens at a specific step, or what causes what", "prompt_sha256": "55efb399f746c2c66d4354e5a73f4fb251e908bfdcc74334d2588416d38e4a89", "generated_at": "2026-08-02T19:24:05Z", "status": "live"}
{"id": "h2-2C-03", "topic": "2C", "stem": "A cell with extensively damaged DNA activates a regulated pathway leading to programmed cell death rather than completing division. Which cellular process is occurring?", "options": ["mitosis", "cytokinesis", "karyokinesis", "apoptosis"], "answer": "apoptosis", "source_id": "27082fea-78ab-5c36-9347-11c9fdedd944", "source_span": {"chunk_id": "27082fea-78ab-5c36-9347-11c9fdedd944#4580-5797", "start": 4748, "end": 4757, "quote": "apoptosis", "block_id": "fs-id1565777", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/10-key-terms"}, "citation": "27082fea-78ab-5c36-9347-11c9fdedd944[4748:4757] https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/10-key-terms#fs-id1565777", "generator": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-2025-08-07", "attempt_id": "2133559d357e", "target_concept": "Programmed cell death", "question_type": "a discrimination question - which of two similar things the described case is", "prompt_sha256": "d5e74c553cc9cdf7bda684645770a637718534ab0f4cf2da0b1a1edd445c9b75", "generated_at": "2026-08-02T19:24:05Z", "status": "live"}
{"id": "h2-3A-02", "topic": "3A", "stem": "Neurotransmitters released by the nervous system primarily regulate which types of target cells?", "options": ["glial cells, adipocytes, and lymphocytes", "neurons, muscle cells, and endocrine cells", "fibroblasts, chondrocytes, and pancreatic cells", "hepatocytes, osteocytes, and epithelial cells"], "answer": "neurons, muscle cells, and endocrine cells", "source_id": "a708d3cb-ec37-4cbb-a945-e0b5fb0be2fa", "source_span": {"chunk_id": "a708d3cb-ec37-4cbb-a945-e0b5fb0be2fa#0-716", "start": 517, "end": 559, "quote": "neurons, muscle cells, and endocrine cells", "block_id": "fs-idp75505792", "url": "https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/37-5-endocrine-glands"}, "citation": "a708d3cb-ec37-4cbb-a945-e0b5fb0be2fa[517:559] https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/37-5-endocrine-glands#fs-idp75505792", "generator": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-2025-08-07", "attempt_id": "f63c3cd39cb0", "target_concept": "Synaptic activity: transmitter molecules", "question_type": "a function question - what the named thing does, or what it is for", "prompt_sha256": "985979e321f079e53976cf204f8016dd0392e712379299b2f82b7ea386e95a20", "generated_at": "2026-08-02T19:24:10Z", "status": "live"}
{"id": "h2-3B-01", "topic": "3B", "stem": "Which term describes the two-circuit pattern of blood flow—pulmonary and systemic—enabled by a four-chambered heart?", "options": ["double circulation", "cardiac output", "coronary artery", "closed circulatory system"], "answer": "double circulation", "source_id": "51255f27-74cd-5fc1-90aa-5a3631baff49", "source_span": {"chunk_id": "51255f27-74cd-5fc1-90aa-5a3631baff49#1116-2216", "start": 1988, "end": 2006, "quote": "double circulation", "block_id": null, "url": "https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/40-key-terms"}, "citation": "51255f27-74cd-5fc1-90aa-5a3631baff49[1988:2006] https://openstax.org/books/biology/pages/40-key-terms", "generator": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-2025-08-07", "attempt_id": "0eca712385e0", "target_concept": "Four-chambered heart: structure and function", "question_type": "an identification question - name the structure, molecule or term the passage describes", "prompt_sha256": "ce49541ef39576040aeaef9a7896d26db68bae36744c415c783dca828f864f1b", "generated_at": "2026-08-02T19:24:19Z", "status": "live"}
